 "findings": [
  {
   "heading": "Descriptive tables (intro)",
   "segment_index": "S1.P2",
   "kind": "untrue",
   "en_span": "chapters/tables_descriptive.qmd:21-21",
   "tr_span": "chapters/tables_descriptive.jp.qmd:21-21",
   "proposition": "The English says tabyl() from janitor is used to PRODUCE tabulations and cross-tabulations (as well as adorn them); the Japanese says tabyl() is used to 'adorn' tabulations and cross-tabulations that have already been created, dropping the producing role.",
   "reader_consequence": "A Japanese reader scanning the tool-choice list concludes tabyl() only decorates an existing table, so they look for some other janitor function to build the tabulation and may not reach for tabyl() at all.",
   "confidence": "medium"
  },
  {
   "heading": "Summary statistics (Browse data)",
   "segment_index": "S7.P3",
   "kind": "untrue",
   "en_span": "chapters/tables_descriptive.qmd:127-127",
   "tr_span": "chapters/tables_descriptive.jp.qmd:119-119",
   "proposition": "The English attributes get_summary_stats() to the rstatix package only; the Japanese sentence reads '**rstatix** gtsummaryの `get_summary_stats()`', attributing the function to gtsummary as well.",
   "reader_consequence": "A Japanese reader may load gtsummary expecting get_summary_stats() from it, or be unsure which package provides the function, and be confused when only rstatix supplies it.",
   "confidence": "high"
  },
  {
   "heading": "Simple tabyl",
   "segment_index": "S9.P1",
   "kind": "untrue",
   "en_span": "chapters/tables_descriptive.qmd:149-149",
   "tr_span": "chapters/tables_descriptive.jp.qmd:137-137",
   "proposition": "The English says the default use of tabyl() is on a specific COLUMN; the Japanese says it is used on a specific ROW ('特定の行に対して `tabyl()` を使用すると').",
   "reader_consequence": "A Japanese reader is told tabyl() operates on a row, which contradicts the adjacent code `linelist %>% tabyl(age_cat)` where age_cat is a column, so they may try to pass a row identifier and fail.",
   "confidence": "high"
  },
  {
   "heading": "Simple tabyl",
   "segment_index": "S9.P1",
   "kind": "untrue",
   "en_span": "chapters/tables_descriptive.qmd:149-149",
   "tr_span": "chapters/tables_descriptive.jp.qmd:137-137",
   "proposition": "The English says the percents tabyl() returns are COLUMN-WISE ('column-wise \"percents\"'); the Japanese says they are per-row ('行ごとの「パーセンテージ」').",
   "reader_consequence": "A Japanese reader misunderstands the denominator of the proportion column produced by tabyl(), and may misread the printed output or wrongly expect row-wise percentages in the cross-tabulation examples that follow.",
   "confidence": "high"
  },
  {
   "heading": "Convert to data frame",
   "segment_index": "S39.P1",
   "kind": "untrue",
   "en_span": "chapters/tables_descriptive.qmd:990-990",
   "tr_span": "chapters/tables_descriptive.jp.qmd:979-979",
   "proposition": "The English step 4 says rownames_to_column() takes the name for the first COLUMN; the Japanese says it specifies the name of the first ROW ('最初の行の名前を指定します').",
   "reader_consequence": "A Japanese reader misreads what `var = \"Age Category\"` does in the chunk beside it, and may expect the string to become a row label instead of the new first column's header.",
   "confidence": "high"
  },
  {
   "heading": "Proportions (dplyr)",
   "segment_index": "S20.P1",
